WEBVTT

00:00:08.128 --> 00:00:12.520
Iris Press Publishers, Humpty and His Family.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.483
By Yulia Puchkova.

00:00:16.543 --> 00:00:22.366
Chapter 1 Life in the Egg.

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:24.928
Hello.

00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:27.368
I'm an ostrich.

00:00:27.428 --> 00:00:30.100
I'm from Africa.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.072
I live in the grasslands.

00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:35.758
Now I'm grown up.

00:00:35.818 --> 00:00:41.196
But I want to start my story from the very beginning.

00:00:41.256 --> 00:00:43.938
Here it is.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:48.022
I'm sitting in an egg.

00:00:48.082 --> 00:00:52.074
It is big, and I'm big too.

00:00:52.134 --> 00:00:55.107
I'm tired of sitting here.

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:57.878
I want to get out.

00:00:57.938 --> 00:01:04.211
I hit the egg with my beak, but nothing happens.

00:01:04.271 --> 00:01:09.442
It is sometimes light and sometimes dark in the egg.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.824
When it is dark, I sleep.

00:01:12.884 --> 00:01:18.157
When it is light, I want to go out.

00:01:18.216 --> 00:01:21.818
Now it is very light.

00:01:21.878 --> 00:01:25.930
I hit the egg with my beak again.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:32.994
Suddenly, there is a small hole in the wall of the egg.

00:01:33.054 --> 00:01:39.380
I take my beak out of the hole and put my eye to it.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.031
I'm looking through the hole now.

00:01:42.051 --> 00:01:48.106
Wow, it's great there.

00:01:48.166 --> 00:01:55.252
I can see a lot of green grass, some green trees and bushes.

00:01:55.312 --> 00:01:58.264
There are different animals.

00:01:58.324 --> 00:02:01.596
They are walking in the grass.

00:02:01.655 --> 00:02:05.367
Some animals are eating the grass.

00:02:05.427 --> 00:02:09.579
Some animals are eating the leaves.

00:02:09.639 --> 00:02:12.420
I can see a cheater.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.222
It is lying in the tall grass.

00:02:16.282 --> 00:02:20.104
It is hiding from a zebra.

00:02:20.164 --> 00:02:25.016
The cheater looks very hungry.

00:02:25.076 --> 00:02:27.270
Oh no!

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:30.606
It wants to eat the zebra.

00:02:30.666 --> 00:02:32.797
I look at the zebra.

00:02:32.857 --> 00:02:35.058
It is eating grass.

00:02:35.118 --> 00:02:38.330
It doesn't see the cheetah.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.542
I'm very angry.

00:02:41.602 --> 00:02:44.284
I want to get out.

00:02:44.344 --> 00:02:47.176
I shake the egg.

00:02:47.236 --> 00:02:52.250
Suddenly, the egg starts rolling.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:57.639
It is rolling and rolling, and I'm rolling too.

00:02:57.699 --> 00:02:59.795
Bang!

00:02:59.855 --> 00:03:04.116
The egg hits the cheater on the back.

00:03:04.176 --> 00:03:09.117
The cheater jumps up, turns around and looks at me.

00:03:09.177 --> 00:03:13.158
Of course, it can't see me.

00:03:13.218 --> 00:03:16.338
It can see only the egg.

00:03:16.398 --> 00:03:19.279
It looks and looks.

00:03:19.339 --> 00:03:23.830
And shows me it's big, ugly teeth.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.132
I'm afraid.

00:03:26.192 --> 00:03:28.843
I'm not looking at it now.

00:03:28.903 --> 00:03:32.144
I'm hiding inside the egg.

00:03:32.204 --> 00:03:35.334
I'm very quiet.

00:03:35.394 --> 00:03:44.977
The cheetah smells the egg, sneezes and walks away.

00:03:45.036 --> 00:03:48.867
I turn the egg.

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:52.178
I can see the zebra now.

00:03:52.238 --> 00:03:55.956
It is running away.

00:03:56.016 --> 00:03:59.486
Oh no!

00:03:59.546 --> 00:04:03.229
Somebody's rolling me back.

00:04:03.289 --> 00:04:05.900
But I know her.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.112
She is my mum.

00:04:08.172 --> 00:04:10.144
She is big and strong.

00:04:10.204 --> 00:04:12.796
She's very tall too.

00:04:12.855 --> 00:04:15.508
Now I'm at home again.

00:04:15.568 --> 00:04:18.180
There are three eggs around me.

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:22.192
There is my brother and two sisters inside them.

00:04:22.252 --> 00:04:24.284
It is dark now.

00:04:24.343 --> 00:04:27.020
I can hear my dad.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.434
He comes home every evening.

00:04:30.494 --> 00:04:33.245
He helps my mum a lot.

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:36.526
He sits on the nest at night.

00:04:36.585 --> 00:04:40.206
Now Dad is sitting down on the nest.

00:04:40.266 --> 00:04:42.326
It is very dark.

00:04:42.386 --> 00:04:45.717
I am tired and I sleep.

00:04:45.777 --> 00:04:57.226
Chapter 2 There are two others.

00:04:57.286 --> 00:05:03.576
I wake up and open my eyes.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.078
It is light again.

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:10.362
I look through the hole and see another egg.

00:05:10.422 --> 00:05:13.324
There is a hole in that egg too.

00:05:13.383 --> 00:05:16.396
There is an eye in the hole.

00:05:16.456 --> 00:05:18.697
We are looking at each other.

00:05:18.757 --> 00:05:22.270
Now the eye winks at me.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.842
I wink too.

00:05:24.902 --> 00:05:29.802
I shake the egg and it starts rolling.

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:32.512
My brother does the same.

00:05:32.572 --> 00:05:37.554
I'm rolling to my brother, and he is rolling to me.

00:05:37.614 --> 00:05:41.496
There is a terrible noise.

00:05:41.556 --> 00:05:47.010
The eggs are a lot of white pieces now, and we are out.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.730
We are free.

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.372
We are lying on the grass.

00:05:51.432 --> 00:05:55.225
I put up my beak and say it to my brother.

00:05:55.284 --> 00:05:57.840
Hello.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:02.226
Hello, he answers.

00:06:02.285 --> 00:06:05.427
Our daddy is next to us.

00:06:05.486 --> 00:06:08.758
Hi, sons, he says.

00:06:08.818 --> 00:06:12.280
Let's give you names.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.650
He turns away and cries.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.282
Dear, come here.

00:06:18.342 --> 00:06:20.222
We've got two sons.

00:06:20.282 --> 00:06:23.277
We must give them names.

00:06:23.337 --> 00:06:28.894
This is the first time I can see our mother in the light.

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:32.516
She is big and strong like our father.

00:06:32.576 --> 00:06:35.059
She is beautiful too.

00:06:35.118 --> 00:06:45.395
She looks at us, winks at our dad and says, Let's call them Humpty and Dumpty.

00:06:45.455 --> 00:06:50.468
Okay, says dad, but who is Humpty?

00:06:50.528 --> 00:06:55.940
Our mum looks at us again, she thinks and says, let's ask them.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:00.552
So, which of you is humpty?

00:07:00.612 --> 00:07:03.553
Me, we answer together.

00:07:03.613 --> 00:07:05.604
No, says our mum.

00:07:05.664 --> 00:07:08.144
Only one can be humpty.

00:07:08.204 --> 00:07:12.746
Then I am dumpedy, we say together.

00:07:12.806 --> 00:07:15.710
My dear, says mum.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.935
We have got a problem with their names.

00:07:18.995 --> 00:07:22.950
But we have got very good sons.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.812
Okay.

00:07:24.872 --> 00:07:27.205
You are Humpty.

00:07:27.265 --> 00:07:28.686
She points at me.

00:07:28.746 --> 00:07:31.190
And you are Dumpty.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.957
She points at my brother.

00:07:34.017 --> 00:07:37.863
Now meet each other, says Dad.

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:42.194
Hello, I say to my brother, I'm Humpty.

00:07:42.254 --> 00:07:44.945
Nice to meet you, he says.

00:07:45.005 --> 00:07:46.756
I'm Dumpty.

00:07:46.816 --> 00:07:49.877
Nice to meet you too, I say.

00:07:49.937 --> 00:07:52.298
And we shake wings.

00:07:52.357 --> 00:08:00.874
Good chicks, say our parents, and smile.

00:08:00.934 --> 00:08:09.982
Chapter 3, Naughty Legs.

00:08:10.042 --> 00:08:14.986
Dumpedie and I are lying on the grass.

00:08:15.046 --> 00:08:18.388
Dad is looking at us.

00:08:18.448 --> 00:08:23.052
It's time to get up, he says.

00:08:23.112 --> 00:08:24.713
I get up.

00:08:24.772 --> 00:08:29.797
Now I'm standing, but my legs don't want to stand.

00:08:29.856 --> 00:08:32.018
They are shaking.

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:35.174
I fall down on the grass.

00:08:35.234 --> 00:08:39.148
Dumpty is laughing.

00:08:39.208 --> 00:08:43.519
It's your turn now, says Dad.

00:08:43.579 --> 00:08:47.060
Dumpty stops laughing.

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:49.620
Now he gets up.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.281
But his legs are like mine.

00:08:52.341 --> 00:08:55.512
They start shaking and he falls down too.

00:08:55.572 --> 00:08:57.212
He's laughing again.

00:08:57.272 --> 00:08:58.843
Why are you laughing?

00:08:58.903 --> 00:09:00.213
Asks Dad.

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.064
You can't walk.

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:04.485
It isn't funny.

00:09:04.545 --> 00:09:09.228
But my legs don't listen to me, laughs dumpty.

00:09:09.288 --> 00:09:10.968
Of course they don't.

00:09:11.028 --> 00:09:14.530
They haven't got any ears, I say, to dumpty.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:18.892
Dad looks at me, then, at his legs.

00:09:18.952 --> 00:09:24.654
I haven't got any ears on my legs, but I can walk, he says.

00:09:24.714 --> 00:09:29.416
It is interesting, I think, and think.

00:09:29.476 --> 00:09:32.774
Suddenly, I have an idea.

00:09:32.834 --> 00:09:37.122
It is because you listen to your legs, I say.

00:09:37.182 --> 00:09:40.374
You walk when they want to walk.

00:09:40.434 --> 00:09:43.336
Mmm, says Dad.

00:09:43.396 --> 00:09:45.837
What about your legs?

00:09:45.897 --> 00:09:48.938
Don't they want to walk?

00:09:48.998 --> 00:09:53.426
Don't you and I listen to our legs.

00:09:53.486 --> 00:09:57.982
No, they don't, we say together.

00:09:58.041 --> 00:10:02.344
But there are a lot of angry animals around us.

00:10:02.404 --> 00:10:06.906
If you can't run, they can catch and eat you.

00:10:06.966 --> 00:10:08.797
How can they do it?

00:10:08.857 --> 00:10:10.388
Asks dumpty.

00:10:10.448 --> 00:10:13.008
You are always with us.

00:10:13.068 --> 00:10:17.421
Sometimes I sleep, says Dad.

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.702
Then there is mum, I say.

00:10:20.762 --> 00:10:25.110
She sometimes sleeps too, says Dad.

00:10:25.171 --> 00:10:33.298
You can always do it in turn, we say together.

00:10:33.358 --> 00:10:41.770
Chapter four, an ungrateful animal.

00:10:41.830 --> 00:10:45.161
It is a great day today.

00:10:45.221 --> 00:10:48.642
Dumpters and my legs want to walk.

00:10:48.702 --> 00:10:50.202
They like it.

00:10:50.262 --> 00:10:52.452
They start running.

00:10:52.512 --> 00:10:56.499
But we always fall down.

00:10:56.559 --> 00:11:00.326
Dad and Mum are happy.

00:11:00.386 --> 00:11:04.360
They're looking at us and smiling.

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:07.582
I start running again.

00:11:07.642 --> 00:11:11.054
Suddenly I can see a zebra.

00:11:11.114 --> 00:11:13.406
I look and look.

00:11:13.466 --> 00:11:14.987
I know it.

00:11:15.047 --> 00:11:16.778
It is my zebra.

00:11:16.838 --> 00:11:18.829
I run to it.

00:11:18.890 --> 00:11:21.612
Hello, I say.

00:11:21.671 --> 00:11:25.064
I know you, but you don't know me.

00:11:25.124 --> 00:11:27.291
I'm Humpty.

00:11:27.351 --> 00:11:34.559
The zebra looks at me and says, But I don't want to know you.

00:11:34.619 --> 00:11:37.930
Why, I ask?

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:51.010
It is because we, zebras, are beautiful, clever animals, and you, ostriches, are ugly, silly birds.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:54.517
Suddenly I can see dumpty.

00:11:54.577 --> 00:11:56.418
He is next to me now.

00:11:56.478 --> 00:11:59.922
He can hear the zebra's words too.

00:11:59.982 --> 00:12:07.398
First, clever animals don't say bad things about other animals.

00:12:07.458 --> 00:12:10.360
Second, you aren't beautiful.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.773
You've got a short thick neck, says he.

00:12:13.833 --> 00:12:16.866
And no feathers, I say.

00:12:16.926 --> 00:12:20.397
The zebra is angry.

00:12:20.457 --> 00:12:25.897
It wants to hit us and it runs at us.

00:12:25.957 --> 00:12:28.408
What is it?

00:12:28.468 --> 00:12:31.278
Our legs want to run too.

00:12:31.338 --> 00:12:35.029
Now we are running very fast.

00:12:35.089 --> 00:12:41.950
Suddenly our legs turn left and the zebra turns left too.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:44.711
It almost falls.

00:12:44.771 --> 00:12:48.746
Then our legs turn right.

00:12:48.806 --> 00:12:52.192
The zebra can't turn so fast.

00:12:52.252 --> 00:12:54.493
It falls down on the ground.

00:12:54.553 --> 00:12:57.784
Its legs are up in the air.

00:12:57.844 --> 00:12:59.824
We ask, sorry.

00:12:59.884 --> 00:13:01.365
We can't help you.

00:13:01.425 --> 00:13:03.185
You're too heavy, too.

00:13:03.245 --> 00:13:06.836
We cry to it and run away.

00:13:06.897 --> 00:13:09.887
We come to our parents.

00:13:09.948 --> 00:13:13.378
Dad, mum, we can run now.

00:13:13.438 --> 00:13:19.031
And when we're running very fast, we can certainly turn left or right.

00:13:19.091 --> 00:13:23.294
It is very good, say dad and mum.

00:13:23.353 --> 00:13:26.074
Only ostriches can do that.

00:13:26.134 --> 00:13:30.246
Do you want to know our teacher, we ask?

00:13:30.306 --> 00:13:32.657
Yes, they say.

00:13:32.717 --> 00:13:34.308
Who is it?

00:13:34.368 --> 00:13:38.539
It is that funny animal in the striped costume.

00:13:38.559 --> 00:13:52.564
Chapter 5 What a name.

00:13:52.624 --> 00:13:56.496
It is very hot today.

00:13:56.555 --> 00:14:01.878
Our parents are standing, and we are lying on the grass.

00:14:01.938 --> 00:14:05.320
We are waiting for our sisters.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:08.841
They are still inside the eggs.

00:14:08.901 --> 00:14:11.552
Mum and Dad are worried.

00:14:11.612 --> 00:14:16.204
Our sisters must come out, but they don't.

00:14:16.264 --> 00:14:18.408
Can we help them?

00:14:18.468 --> 00:14:20.453
My brother and I ask.

00:14:20.513 --> 00:14:23.174
We can't help them, says Dad.

00:14:23.234 --> 00:14:25.746
They must do it themselves.

00:14:25.806 --> 00:14:30.698
I'm sure they're girls, says Dumpty.

00:14:30.758 --> 00:14:35.050
How do you know, asks Dad?

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.350
They're not strong.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.282
Answers my brother.

00:14:39.342 --> 00:14:42.593
Yes, they're weak, I say.

00:14:42.653 --> 00:14:44.404
We must help them.

00:14:44.464 --> 00:14:47.940
I'm sure they can't get out themselves.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.758
Suddenly we can hear a noise.

00:14:51.818 --> 00:14:55.702
There are two holes in one of the eggs.

00:14:55.762 --> 00:15:00.616
I can see two beautiful brown eyes in the holes.

00:15:00.676 --> 00:15:03.088
They are looking at me.

00:15:03.148 --> 00:15:06.972
Hello, I say, I'm Humpty.

00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:08.022
And who are you?

00:15:08.042 --> 00:15:12.586
Mmm, says the egg.

00:15:12.646 --> 00:15:15.480
Then there is a loud noise again.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:17.642
And there is no egg now.

00:15:17.702 --> 00:15:21.634
There is a beautiful chick in front of us.

00:15:21.694 --> 00:15:24.874
Of course, it is a girl.

00:15:24.934 --> 00:15:27.105
She is our sister.

00:15:27.165 --> 00:15:33.836
She has got very soft, long feathers and a long, sporty neck.

00:15:33.897 --> 00:15:38.648
Let's call her beauty, says Mum.

00:15:38.708 --> 00:15:41.858
No, says my sister.

00:15:41.918 --> 00:15:44.529
I don't like this name.

00:15:44.589 --> 00:15:47.932
What about feathery?"

00:15:47.992 --> 00:15:49.742
asks Dad.

00:15:49.802 --> 00:15:52.996
No, she says again.

00:15:53.056 --> 00:16:02.094
At this moment we can hear a terrible noise, and our other sister comes out of the egg.

00:16:02.154 --> 00:16:05.446
She is very beautiful too.

00:16:05.507 --> 00:16:07.458
But she is small.

00:16:07.518 --> 00:16:09.580
She is smiling at us.

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:13.096
A smile is so nice and kind.

00:16:13.156 --> 00:16:16.069
Hello, smiley, I say.

00:16:16.129 --> 00:16:18.600
Nice to meet you.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:22.751
Smiley, she cries and smiles again.

00:16:22.771 --> 00:16:24.452
I like it.

00:16:24.512 --> 00:16:26.482
It's a nice name.

00:16:26.542 --> 00:16:29.074
Good girl, says Mum.

00:16:29.134 --> 00:16:31.584
But we have a problem with your sister.

00:16:31.644 --> 00:16:34.686
We can't find a name for her.

00:16:34.746 --> 00:16:37.876
Let's ask her, says smiley.

00:16:37.936 --> 00:16:39.937
What's your name?

00:16:39.997 --> 00:16:47.881
Our big sister looks around and sees a very beautiful dragonfly.

00:16:47.941 --> 00:16:50.042
What is this?

00:16:50.102 --> 00:16:51.844
She asks.

00:16:51.904 --> 00:16:55.646
It's a dragonfly, says Mum.

00:16:55.706 --> 00:17:02.109
Then my name is Dragonfly, says our sister.

00:17:02.169 --> 00:17:06.832
Oh, it's a very long name, says Dad.

00:17:06.892 --> 00:17:09.281
We must make it short.

00:17:09.341 --> 00:17:12.400
We can call you fly.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.382
Or dragon says dumpty.

00:17:16.442 --> 00:17:22.186
But I don't want to have a dragon in the family, cries dad.

00:17:22.246 --> 00:17:29.210
And I want to be a dragon, says our sister, and stamps.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.552
Okay, says mum.

00:17:32.612 --> 00:17:34.774
Be dragon if you like.

00:17:34.834 --> 00:17:41.812
And she winks at dad.

00:17:41.872 --> 00:17:55.881
Chapter 6 Strange grown-ups Today we are going out into the world.

00:17:55.941 --> 00:18:00.762
It is the first time Dad and Mum take us with them.

00:18:00.822 --> 00:18:03.583
We walk together.

00:18:03.643 --> 00:18:08.474
Then we see two very big ostriches.

00:18:08.534 --> 00:18:11.274
They are walking too.

00:18:11.335 --> 00:18:14.002
They are coming to us.

00:18:14.062 --> 00:18:18.471
Now we can see three small chicks with them.

00:18:18.532 --> 00:18:21.602
They are all girls.

00:18:21.663 --> 00:18:24.564
Our parents stop.

00:18:24.624 --> 00:18:27.766
They talk to the big ostriches.

00:18:27.826 --> 00:18:32.307
They say, oh, what beautiful daughters you have got.

00:18:32.367 --> 00:18:40.211
Their necks are so long, their feathers are so soft, their beaks are so thick.

00:18:40.271 --> 00:19:03.007
The big ostriches smile and say, And your daughters are so cute, They've got long legs and small bodies, Their smiles are so nice, And your sons are so strong, Their eyes are so clever, Their heads are so round.

00:19:03.067 --> 00:19:13.716
I look at my brother, At his eyes and head, And I say, That is not true.

00:19:13.776 --> 00:19:17.707
We can't be strong because we're very small.

00:19:17.767 --> 00:19:21.668
We can't be clever because we're very young.

00:19:21.728 --> 00:19:26.180
And our heads aren't round because they are square.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:29.160
Why do you say that?

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:31.901
Dad is looking at me.

00:19:31.961 --> 00:19:33.952
I can feel that.

00:19:34.012 --> 00:19:37.003
And he is very angry.

00:19:37.063 --> 00:19:38.503
But why?

00:19:38.563 --> 00:19:46.442
I look at him and ask, Why are you angry with me?

00:19:46.502 --> 00:19:51.384
Because you are rude, my son, he answers.

00:19:51.444 --> 00:19:54.056
Why am I rude?

00:19:54.116 --> 00:19:57.278
I don't know, he says.

00:19:57.338 --> 00:20:04.692
I think it is because you are too small, too young, and your head is too square.

00:20:04.712 --> 00:20:09.270
I don't understand my dad.

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:17.794
Sometimes grown-ups are so strange.

00:20:17.854 --> 00:20:28.182
Chapter 7 Why does she run away?

00:20:28.242 --> 00:20:33.086
I'm hot and very thirsty.

00:20:33.146 --> 00:20:39.095
I come up to Dad and say, Dad, I'm hot and thirsty.

00:20:39.155 --> 00:20:42.782
Can we go and find water?

00:20:42.842 --> 00:20:46.296
Okay, says Dad.

00:20:46.356 --> 00:20:52.251
Hide under my wings, and tell your brother and sisters to hide there too.

00:20:52.312 --> 00:20:58.106
Hey, dumpedy, smiley, dragon, come here.

00:20:58.166 --> 00:21:01.710
It's cool under Dad's wings, I cry.

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:06.442
They run to us, and soon we're all together.

00:21:06.502 --> 00:21:12.001
Let's play, hide and seek, says Dumpty.

00:21:12.062 --> 00:21:15.194
Let's, we say.

00:21:15.254 --> 00:21:20.645
Humpty, you must look for us, says Dragon.

00:21:20.706 --> 00:21:22.246
Why not?

00:21:22.306 --> 00:21:24.668
I close my eyes.

00:21:24.728 --> 00:21:31.000
It is very funny to hide in Dad's feathers or between his legs.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:36.458
First I find Dumpty, then I find Smiley.

00:21:36.518 --> 00:21:39.524
Oh, I can't find Dragon.

00:21:39.584 --> 00:21:41.514
Where is she?

00:21:41.575 --> 00:21:45.676
Suddenly we can hear a small voice.

00:21:45.736 --> 00:21:49.488
Hello, can I play with you?

00:21:49.548 --> 00:21:53.279
We look and see a cute ostrich girl.

00:21:53.338 --> 00:21:57.630
I like her, and I say, of course you can.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.390
Can you help me?

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:02.142
Yes, she says and smiles.

00:22:02.202 --> 00:22:04.030
What must I do?

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:08.031
We must find Dragon, I answer.

00:22:08.091 --> 00:22:13.195
The girl starts shaking, then she cries.

00:22:13.255 --> 00:22:15.528
Mummy!

00:22:15.588 --> 00:22:18.510
And runs away.

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:22.674
I look at Dumpty and smiley.

00:22:22.734 --> 00:22:26.707
Why doesn't she want to find Dragon, I ask?

00:22:26.767 --> 00:22:29.762
We don't know, they answer.

00:22:29.822 --> 00:22:35.616
Now we are looking for dragon together, but we can't find her.

00:22:35.676 --> 00:22:39.509
Suddenly, I can see dragon.

00:22:39.569 --> 00:22:43.821
She is running between mum's legs and laughing at us.

00:22:43.881 --> 00:22:48.453
I'm very clever, she cries.

00:22:48.514 --> 00:22:53.076
Soon, we come to a big river.

00:22:53.136 --> 00:22:58.150
There are a lot of animals next to the river.

00:22:58.211 --> 00:23:01.294
They are drinking water.

00:23:01.354 --> 00:23:06.340
There are antelopes, giraffes and elephants.

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:09.342
They are big, but kind.

00:23:09.402 --> 00:23:11.914
There are lions too.

00:23:11.974 --> 00:23:15.958
Dad says they are angry.

00:23:16.018 --> 00:23:17.910
I look at Dad.

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.221
He isn't afraid of lions.

00:23:20.282 --> 00:23:23.000
He is very brave.

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:27.140
We come up to the river and drink.

00:23:27.201 --> 00:23:31.443
The water is tasty and cool.

00:23:31.503 --> 00:23:34.645
I want to play with the water.

00:23:34.705 --> 00:23:36.746
I go into the river.

00:23:36.806 --> 00:23:41.860
Humpty, you mustn't wet your body, cries mum.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:44.142
Only your legs.

00:23:44.202 --> 00:23:47.324
My legs are in the water now.

00:23:47.384 --> 00:23:49.745
Smiley is looking at me.

00:23:49.805 --> 00:23:52.214
She is afraid.

00:23:52.274 --> 00:23:55.725
Smiley, come here I cry.

00:23:55.785 --> 00:23:58.347
The water is soft and kind.

00:23:58.407 --> 00:24:00.909
My legs like it.

00:24:00.969 --> 00:24:03.782
Smiley goes into the water.

00:24:03.842 --> 00:24:05.432
She likes it.

00:24:05.492 --> 00:24:08.175
Dumpity is in the water too.

00:24:08.235 --> 00:24:12.278
Now all our legs are in the water.

00:24:12.338 --> 00:24:17.402
Suddenly we can hear the small voice again.

00:24:17.462 --> 00:24:19.950
Can I play with you?

00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:25.039
I turn round and see that cute ostrich girl.

00:24:25.100 --> 00:24:28.762
I'm happy to see you again, I say.

00:24:28.822 --> 00:24:30.554
Let's play together.

00:24:30.614 --> 00:24:31.844
I'm humpty.

00:24:31.904 --> 00:24:35.807
This is smiley and that is dumpty.

00:24:35.867 --> 00:24:38.710
Nice to meet you.

00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:44.264
I'm softy, says the girl and smiles.

00:24:44.324 --> 00:24:46.716
Wait, say smiley.

00:24:46.776 --> 00:24:48.267
We can't start playing.

00:24:48.327 --> 00:24:50.140
We must call dragon.

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.042
Dragon, we cry.

00:24:52.102 --> 00:24:53.993
Dragon, come here.

00:24:54.053 --> 00:24:55.483
There she is.

00:24:55.543 --> 00:24:57.844
Dragon is running to us.

00:24:57.904 --> 00:24:59.414
Dragon, I say.

00:24:59.474 --> 00:25:01.304
We've got a friend.

00:25:01.364 --> 00:25:04.795
Her name is Softy.

00:25:04.855 --> 00:25:09.786
I turn my head, but there is no Softy.

00:25:09.846 --> 00:25:12.177
Where is your friend?

00:25:12.237 --> 00:25:14.445
Asks Dragon.

00:25:14.505 --> 00:25:19.435
I don't know, I say, and look around.

00:25:19.495 --> 00:25:22.917
Suddenly, I can see Softie.

00:25:22.977 --> 00:25:27.349
She's running away, very fast.

00:25:27.409 --> 00:25:30.020
I'm very sad.

00:25:30.080 --> 00:25:33.872
I don't know why, but I like Softie.

00:25:33.933 --> 00:25:36.943
I think she's very strange.

00:25:37.004 --> 00:25:43.257
First, she wants to play with us, but then she always runs away.

00:25:43.277 --> 00:25:48.578
Why?

00:25:48.638 --> 00:26:04.130
Chapter 8 Living Stones We are standing with our legs in the river.

00:26:04.190 --> 00:26:08.164
Dragon is looking at the water.

00:26:08.224 --> 00:26:19.588
Suddenly she says, Look, there are big brown stones in the water.

00:26:19.648 --> 00:26:27.638
I look at the stones, they are very interesting.

00:26:27.698 --> 00:26:35.454
Dragon, have stones got eyes, I ask.

00:26:35.514 --> 00:26:39.618
Of course they haven't, she answers.

00:26:39.678 --> 00:26:49.414
Dragon, have stones got ears, I ask my second question.

00:26:49.474 --> 00:26:52.026
Of course they haven't!

00:26:52.086 --> 00:26:54.738
You are so silly, Humpty!

00:26:54.798 --> 00:26:56.700
Dragon!

00:26:56.760 --> 00:27:00.643
Have stones got nostrils?

00:27:00.703 --> 00:27:03.666
I ask my third question.

00:27:03.726 --> 00:27:12.015
She looks at me, puts her wing to her head, and turns it there three times.

00:27:12.075 --> 00:27:29.633
Then you aren't standing on a stone, I say, because your stone is looking at me and listening to us, and it has got a big nose.

00:27:29.693 --> 00:27:37.868
Christ, dragon, you are too hot.

00:27:37.928 --> 00:27:44.979
Turn your head down, and look, I say.

00:27:45.039 --> 00:27:54.241
Now, Dragon is looking at the stone under her toes, and the stone is looking at her.

00:27:54.302 --> 00:27:56.492
Their eyes meet.

00:27:56.552 --> 00:27:59.243
Dragon is afraid.

00:27:59.303 --> 00:28:01.554
She is shaking.

00:28:01.614 --> 00:28:06.155
Hello, she whispers.

00:28:06.215 --> 00:28:12.320
Mmm, says the stone.

00:28:12.380 --> 00:28:15.154
Mummy!

00:28:15.174 --> 00:28:22.450
Christ dragon and jumps off the stone.

00:28:22.510 --> 00:28:27.934
The stone starts growing.

00:28:27.994 --> 00:28:31.076
It grows and grows.

00:28:31.136 --> 00:28:38.332
Now it has got a fat body and a very big mouth.

00:28:38.392 --> 00:28:40.385
Hello.

00:28:40.445 --> 00:28:44.740
I'm a hippo," says the stone.

00:28:44.800 --> 00:28:48.444
And I'm dragon, says my sister.

00:28:48.504 --> 00:28:54.268
Dragon asks the hippo and starts shaking.

00:28:54.328 --> 00:28:57.200
Oh, I'm so afraid.

00:28:57.260 --> 00:29:00.352
Please don't eat me, dragon.

00:29:00.412 --> 00:29:06.549
Now he's laughing, but he looks very kind.

00:29:06.610 --> 00:29:09.044
I understand.

00:29:09.104 --> 00:29:12.096
He is playing with Dragon.

00:29:12.156 --> 00:29:15.038
Dragon is very angry.

00:29:15.098 --> 00:29:18.610
She thinks he is laughing at her.

00:29:18.671 --> 00:29:20.722
Let's go, chicks.

00:29:20.782 --> 00:29:26.197
She says to us, it's silly to talk to a stone.

00:29:26.257 --> 00:29:30.480
The hippo can hear her words.

00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:32.762
He stops laughing.

00:29:32.822 --> 00:29:35.494
Now he looks sad.

00:29:35.554 --> 00:29:42.950
He says, That's why we live underwater.

00:29:43.010 --> 00:29:46.422
And he goes under the water again.

00:29:46.442 --> 00:29:51.404
I feel very bad.

00:29:51.464 --> 00:30:00.320
My sister is sometimes so rude.

00:30:00.380 --> 00:30:11.702
Chapter 9 They want to live too.

00:30:11.762 --> 00:30:16.195
I want to see Sophie.

00:30:16.255 --> 00:30:20.968
I want to ask her why she always runs away.

00:30:21.028 --> 00:30:23.620
I look around.

00:30:23.680 --> 00:30:26.772
I can't see her in the river.

00:30:26.832 --> 00:30:30.926
I can't see her near the river.

00:30:30.986 --> 00:30:34.218
I am very sad.

00:30:34.278 --> 00:30:38.389
Let's go home, says Mum.

00:30:38.449 --> 00:30:44.832
We get out of the water and walk home with mum and dad.

00:30:44.892 --> 00:30:51.306
Suddenly, a very small, green animal jumps at me.

00:30:51.366 --> 00:30:53.817
It is very funny.

00:30:53.878 --> 00:31:00.652
It has got four short legs and two very long and strong legs.

00:31:00.712 --> 00:31:05.186
It has got very big, funny eyes too.

00:31:05.246 --> 00:31:06.836
What's this?

00:31:06.896 --> 00:31:08.586
I ask dad.

00:31:08.646 --> 00:31:11.226
It's food, he answers.

00:31:11.286 --> 00:31:13.197
Very tasty food.

00:31:13.257 --> 00:31:14.987
Eat it.

00:31:15.047 --> 00:31:17.698
I look at the animal.

00:31:17.758 --> 00:31:23.539
It is sitting on my left leg and making a funny noise.

00:31:23.599 --> 00:31:25.840
I can't eat it.

00:31:25.900 --> 00:31:29.120
I'm sure it wants to live.

00:31:29.181 --> 00:31:33.681
Suddenly, I can see a big beak.

00:31:33.741 --> 00:31:38.314
The beak opens and catches the animal.

00:31:38.374 --> 00:31:42.056
Oh no, I cry.

00:31:42.116 --> 00:31:44.307
I can see dragon.

00:31:44.367 --> 00:31:48.079
The green animal is inside her beak.

00:31:48.139 --> 00:31:50.150
What are you doing?

00:31:50.210 --> 00:31:51.430
I cry.

00:31:51.490 --> 00:31:53.201
Open your beak.

00:31:53.261 --> 00:31:55.082
Mmm.

00:31:55.143 --> 00:31:58.024
Answers dragon.

00:31:58.084 --> 00:32:03.536
Then I take dragon by the legs and shake her.

00:32:03.596 --> 00:32:09.175
Her beak opens and the green animal jumps out.

00:32:09.235 --> 00:32:12.414
Are you crazy?"

00:32:12.474 --> 00:32:14.234
cried Dragon.

00:32:14.294 --> 00:32:18.297
I'm fine, and you aren't kind, I say.

00:32:18.357 --> 00:32:24.501
Look, there are a lot of seeds and fruit in the grasslands.

00:32:24.562 --> 00:32:27.745
Why do you want to eat an animal?

00:32:27.805 --> 00:32:31.458
Because I like it, says Dragon.

00:32:31.519 --> 00:32:33.730
No, you don't.

00:32:33.790 --> 00:32:39.112
When you like somebody, you want to play with her or talk to her.

00:32:39.172 --> 00:32:42.933
You don't want to eat her.

00:32:42.994 --> 00:32:46.715
Laughs, Dragon.

00:32:46.775 --> 00:32:49.936
Humpty is in love.

00:32:49.996 --> 00:32:53.458
Dumpty, smiley, listen.

00:32:53.518 --> 00:32:56.414
Humpty is in love.

00:32:56.474 --> 00:32:58.188
Who is she?

00:32:58.248 --> 00:33:00.110
Tell us.

00:33:00.170 --> 00:33:04.984
Now, I am very angry.

00:33:05.044 --> 00:33:08.926
I want to hit Dragon, but I can't.

00:33:08.986 --> 00:33:11.558
She's a girl.

00:33:11.618 --> 00:33:14.940
Smiley looks at me.

00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:21.226
She understands me, and she says, I'm in love too.

00:33:21.286 --> 00:33:24.688
It is so nice to be in love.

00:33:24.748 --> 00:33:34.285
My brother, Dumpty, looks at us, then at dragon and says, I'm in love too.

00:33:34.345 --> 00:33:37.888
That's a pity you are not, dragon.

00:33:37.948 --> 00:33:58.668
Chapter 10 When we are together, Today, Mum and Dad are at home and we are not.

00:33:58.728 --> 00:34:01.959
We are walking and looking around.

00:34:02.019 --> 00:34:07.670
It is very interesting in the grassland.

00:34:07.730 --> 00:34:11.970
I look at the grass.

00:34:12.031 --> 00:34:16.592
There are a lot of those green animals there.

00:34:16.652 --> 00:34:20.602
Mum says they are insects.

00:34:20.662 --> 00:34:25.543
My green animal's name is a grasshopper.

00:34:25.604 --> 00:34:28.895
There are other animals too.

00:34:28.956 --> 00:34:36.130
I can see ants, butterflies, spiders and snails.

00:34:36.191 --> 00:34:41.274
Some grasshoppers are jumping, some are singing.

00:34:41.334 --> 00:34:43.826
The ants are working.

00:34:43.885 --> 00:34:45.997
The butterflies are flying.

00:34:46.057 --> 00:34:48.328
The spiders are hunting.

00:34:48.388 --> 00:34:50.883
The snails are lazy.

00:34:50.942 --> 00:34:55.988
They are sleeping on the leaves or grass.

00:34:56.048 --> 00:35:02.734
Together we are watching insects and other animals.

00:35:02.794 --> 00:35:06.396
Only dragon is not with us.

00:35:06.456 --> 00:35:09.879
She doesn't like watching small animals.

00:35:09.939 --> 00:35:12.340
She likes eating them.

00:35:12.400 --> 00:35:15.964
She can even eat a lizard.

00:35:16.024 --> 00:35:18.459
We are very quiet.

00:35:18.519 --> 00:35:23.324
A butterfly sits down on smiley's wing.

00:35:23.384 --> 00:35:26.976
It is so beautiful.

00:35:27.036 --> 00:35:32.468
Suddenly I can feel danger.

00:35:32.528 --> 00:35:39.810
We are watching a butterfly and the lioness is watching us.

00:35:39.870 --> 00:35:44.842
Smiley, dumpty, I whisper.

00:35:44.902 --> 00:35:49.358
There's a lioness behind us.

00:35:49.418 --> 00:35:53.993
She is hiding in the bushes.

00:35:54.053 --> 00:35:56.584
They look at me.

00:35:56.644 --> 00:35:59.774
They are afraid.

00:35:59.834 --> 00:36:02.826
What can we do?

00:36:02.886 --> 00:36:05.386
They whisper to me.

00:36:05.446 --> 00:36:12.152
We must run very fast, and we must stay together.

00:36:12.212 --> 00:36:18.454
Now we are running and the lioness is running after us.

00:36:18.514 --> 00:36:22.313
We can hear her behind us.

00:36:22.373 --> 00:36:27.380
Humpty, she can catch us, cries smiley.

00:36:27.440 --> 00:36:30.273
Suddenly, I have an idea.

00:36:30.333 --> 00:36:32.874
Stop chicks, I cry.

00:36:32.934 --> 00:36:39.580
We must turn with our backs to each other and stand in a circle, wing in wing.

00:36:39.640 --> 00:36:47.408
When the lioness jumps at you, you lie on the backs and kick her with your legs.

00:36:47.468 --> 00:36:50.442
So we stand in a circle.

00:36:50.502 --> 00:36:54.433
I can feel my brothers and sisters' backs behind.

00:36:54.493 --> 00:36:56.834
The lioness runs at me.

00:36:56.894 --> 00:36:59.404
Then she jumps at me.

00:36:59.464 --> 00:37:04.445
I lie on my friend's backs and give her a strong kick.

00:37:04.505 --> 00:37:06.986
The lioness flies away.

00:37:07.046 --> 00:37:10.566
Fly lioness fly.

00:37:10.626 --> 00:37:15.036
Now she is very angry.

00:37:15.096 --> 00:37:17.796
She's running around us.

00:37:17.856 --> 00:37:26.033
But every time when she jumps at us, she gets a strong kick and flies away.

00:37:26.093 --> 00:37:30.136
Then the lioness comes back again.

00:37:30.196 --> 00:37:32.798
It is strange.

00:37:32.858 --> 00:37:36.521
I think she likes flying.

00:37:36.581 --> 00:37:40.134
At last, she's very tired.

00:37:40.194 --> 00:37:42.116
She can't catch us.

00:37:42.176 --> 00:37:46.550
She's still angry, but she walks away.

00:37:46.610 --> 00:37:51.604
Well done, Humpty, say my brother and sister.

00:37:51.664 --> 00:37:55.726
Well done, dumped in smiley, I say.

00:37:55.786 --> 00:37:58.327
We are very proud today.

00:37:58.387 --> 00:38:01.808
We are only small, young ostriches.

00:38:01.868 --> 00:38:10.341
But when we are together, we can fight a lion.

00:38:10.401 --> 00:38:19.642
Chapter 11 A race.

00:38:19.702 --> 00:38:23.535
We are at home again.

00:38:23.595 --> 00:38:26.697
But we don't want to have a rest.

00:38:26.758 --> 00:38:29.060
We want to run and play.

00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:36.585
Dad looks at us, smiles and says, Let's have a race.

00:38:36.645 --> 00:38:41.179
What is a race, I ask?

00:38:41.239 --> 00:38:46.054
It's when all the chicks run together to their mum.

00:38:46.114 --> 00:38:51.068
And one of them comes the first, says Dad.

00:38:51.128 --> 00:38:55.150
I want to be the first, says Dragon.

00:38:55.210 --> 00:38:59.192
I want to be the first two, says Dumpty.

00:38:59.252 --> 00:39:02.183
And I can be the fourth, says Smiley.

00:39:02.243 --> 00:39:04.394
I don't want to be the first.

00:39:04.454 --> 00:39:08.026
And you, Humpty, asks Dad.

00:39:08.086 --> 00:39:09.967
I want to run.

00:39:10.027 --> 00:39:12.855
I like running, I answer.

00:39:12.915 --> 00:39:17.373
Then let's start, stand next to each other.

00:39:17.433 --> 00:39:22.114
One, two, three, go.

00:39:22.174 --> 00:39:25.434
We all start running to mum.

00:39:25.494 --> 00:39:28.995
She's standing very far away.

00:39:29.055 --> 00:39:32.066
Smiley is running the first.

00:39:32.126 --> 00:39:34.316
She's in front of me.

00:39:34.376 --> 00:39:37.367
I look behind and see Dumpty.

00:39:37.427 --> 00:39:39.768
He's the third.

00:39:39.828 --> 00:39:43.497
Then there is Dragon.

00:39:43.557 --> 00:39:47.158
Suddenly, dragon cries.

00:39:47.218 --> 00:39:49.050
Oh my stomach!

00:39:49.110 --> 00:39:51.091
We turn our heads.

00:39:51.151 --> 00:39:54.784
Dragon falls on the ground and starts rolling.

00:39:54.844 --> 00:39:56.826
Oh chicks, help me.

00:39:56.886 --> 00:39:59.918
I've got an awful stomachache.

00:39:59.978 --> 00:40:02.600
We run to dragon.

00:40:02.660 --> 00:40:04.412
She looks terrible.

00:40:04.472 --> 00:40:06.423
All her feathers are dirty.

00:40:06.483 --> 00:40:08.795
Her eyes are closed.

00:40:08.855 --> 00:40:12.722
Suddenly, she opens them.

00:40:12.783 --> 00:40:19.951
Oh dear brothers and sister, help me to get up please, she says.

00:40:20.012 --> 00:40:22.603
We look at each other.

00:40:22.663 --> 00:40:30.007
It is the first time dragon says please, and it is very strange.

00:40:30.068 --> 00:40:33.880
We take her by the wings and help her.

00:40:33.940 --> 00:40:36.742
Thank you, she says.

00:40:36.802 --> 00:40:40.414
Now, stand behind me please.

00:40:40.474 --> 00:40:43.840
I'm afraid I can fall on my back.

00:40:43.900 --> 00:40:46.837
What's the matter with dragon?

00:40:46.897 --> 00:40:49.548
Now she says, thank you.

00:40:49.608 --> 00:40:52.238
I'm sure she is really ill.

00:40:52.298 --> 00:40:55.959
We stand behind her.

00:40:56.019 --> 00:40:57.900
Thank you.

00:40:57.960 --> 00:41:00.150
She says again.

00:41:00.210 --> 00:41:02.931
I think my stomach is okay now.

00:41:02.991 --> 00:41:06.952
One, two, three, go.

00:41:07.012 --> 00:41:09.504
She cries and starts running.

00:41:09.564 --> 00:41:14.878
We look at each other, then we understand everything.

00:41:14.938 --> 00:41:17.050
Naughty dragon.

00:41:17.110 --> 00:41:18.900
We start running too.

00:41:18.960 --> 00:41:23.762
Dragon turns her head and laughs.

00:41:23.822 --> 00:41:28.014
You're too silly, my brothers and sister.

00:41:28.074 --> 00:41:32.777
Suddenly, she's quiet.

00:41:32.837 --> 00:41:38.054
She stops running and sits down on the grass.

00:41:38.114 --> 00:41:42.122
Smiley and I are next to her now.

00:41:42.182 --> 00:41:44.212
We can hear a noise.

00:41:44.272 --> 00:41:46.044
Dragon is coughing.

00:41:46.104 --> 00:41:49.055
Her cough is terrible.

00:41:49.115 --> 00:41:52.587
Now dumpity is with us too.

00:41:52.647 --> 00:41:57.970
We all hit her on the back again and again.

00:41:58.030 --> 00:42:05.402
Suddenly a beautiful big butterfly flies out of her beak.

00:42:05.462 --> 00:42:14.248
Food is escaping, cries dragon and wants to get up but starts coughing again.

00:42:14.308 --> 00:42:21.184
This time an orange dragon fly and a purple fly come out.

00:42:21.244 --> 00:42:25.207
Then a fat grasshopper jumps out.

00:42:25.267 --> 00:42:28.930
Now dragon stops coughing.

00:42:28.990 --> 00:42:36.342
Again that green animal she cries and runs after the poor grasshopper.

00:42:36.402 --> 00:42:40.962
She keeps her mouth open when she's running, says Smiley.

00:42:41.022 --> 00:42:43.464
It's very dangerous.

00:42:43.524 --> 00:42:45.495
Yes, I say.

00:42:45.515 --> 00:42:52.388
Especially for insects.

00:42:52.448 --> 00:43:00.813
Chapter 12 A storm.

00:43:00.874 --> 00:43:03.435
It is afternoon.

00:43:03.495 --> 00:43:05.922
It is very hot.

00:43:05.982 --> 00:43:08.478
We are at home.

00:43:08.538 --> 00:43:11.830
We are hiding under Dad's wings.

00:43:11.890 --> 00:43:14.092
Mum is away.

00:43:14.152 --> 00:43:16.522
What is it?

00:43:16.582 --> 00:43:19.554
The sky isn't blue now.

00:43:19.614 --> 00:43:22.164
It is black.

00:43:22.224 --> 00:43:24.476
What's the matter?

00:43:24.536 --> 00:43:26.736
I ask Dad.

00:43:26.797 --> 00:43:31.028
There are clouds in the sky, says Dad.

00:43:31.089 --> 00:43:33.850
But why is it so dark?

00:43:33.910 --> 00:43:36.051
Ask Stunty.

00:43:36.111 --> 00:43:42.066
It's because the clouds are covering the sun and says, Dad.

00:43:42.126 --> 00:43:47.300
Suddenly, we can feel the air.

00:43:47.360 --> 00:43:51.272
The air is running.

00:43:51.332 --> 00:43:55.575
Is the air afraid of the clouds?

00:43:55.635 --> 00:43:56.736
I ask, Dad.

00:43:56.796 --> 00:43:58.748
Why is it running?

00:43:58.808 --> 00:44:01.880
Dad smiles and answers.

00:44:01.940 --> 00:44:06.113
The running air is the wind.

00:44:06.173 --> 00:44:13.992
I don't know why, but it's always very windy before a storm.

00:44:14.052 --> 00:44:18.807
What is a storm asks Smiley?

00:44:18.867 --> 00:44:21.150
She's shaking.

00:44:21.210 --> 00:44:24.522
She's afraid of the strong wind.

00:44:24.582 --> 00:44:28.132
She doesn't like the black clouds.

00:44:28.192 --> 00:44:34.694
A storm is dead starts and stops.

00:44:34.754 --> 00:44:38.246
I can feel water on my beak.

00:44:38.306 --> 00:44:46.101
Chicks hide under my body, cries dad, and stand next to each other.

00:44:46.161 --> 00:44:49.864
Why must I stand next to them?"

00:44:49.924 --> 00:44:51.606
asks Dragon.

00:44:51.666 --> 00:44:54.367
She doesn't want to listen to Dad.

00:44:54.427 --> 00:44:56.268
Dad is angry.

00:44:56.328 --> 00:44:58.659
Do what I say.

00:44:58.719 --> 00:45:00.520
He cries to Dragon.

00:45:00.580 --> 00:45:04.693
You mustn't walk in the rain.

00:45:04.753 --> 00:45:12.722
This is only water, she says, and runs from under Dad's wing.

00:45:12.782 --> 00:45:18.009
The air isn't hot now, it's cool.

00:45:18.069 --> 00:45:20.980
And the water is cool, too.

00:45:21.040 --> 00:45:23.441
The rain is funny.

00:45:23.501 --> 00:45:26.352
But I must listen to Dad.

00:45:26.412 --> 00:45:32.954
So I don't go to Dragon, Dumpety, and smiley listen to Dad, too.

00:45:33.014 --> 00:45:35.836
There under his body.

00:45:35.896 --> 00:45:40.287
You are afraid of the water, Christ Dragon.

00:45:40.347 --> 00:45:44.980
She is dancing in the rain and laughing at us.

00:45:45.040 --> 00:45:51.874
You remember, when we go to the river, we never wet our bodies.

00:45:51.934 --> 00:46:00.947
Now, dragon is all wet, her head is wet, her body is wet, and her wings are wet.

00:46:01.007 --> 00:46:05.929
The water is running down her beak and her legs.

00:46:05.989 --> 00:46:08.760
We can't see any feathers.

00:46:08.820 --> 00:46:11.410
Where are they?

00:46:11.471 --> 00:46:15.816
Dragon isn't dragon anymore.

00:46:15.876 --> 00:46:18.791
She is thin and ugly.

00:46:18.851 --> 00:46:22.865
Her head is very small now.

00:46:22.925 --> 00:46:27.920
She is shaking, because she is laughing at us.

00:46:27.980 --> 00:46:33.384
When she laughs, we only can see her big open beak.

00:46:33.444 --> 00:46:36.908
It is so big and her neck is so thin.

00:46:36.968 --> 00:46:40.002
We close our eyes and open them again.

00:46:40.062 --> 00:46:42.052
But nothing changes.

00:46:42.112 --> 00:46:44.024
There is no dragon.

00:46:44.084 --> 00:46:47.956
Only that ugly, laughing bird.

00:46:48.016 --> 00:46:52.518
Suddenly, the rain stops.

00:46:52.578 --> 00:46:56.620
But the air is still very cool.

00:46:56.680 --> 00:46:59.862
Soon, our mum comes.

00:46:59.922 --> 00:47:05.394
She looks at the bird and cries, Who is that?

00:47:05.454 --> 00:47:08.896
That's Dragon answers Dad.

00:47:08.956 --> 00:47:13.758
Our Dragon asks Mum and her beak opens.

00:47:13.818 --> 00:47:17.410
Of course, ours says Dad.

00:47:17.470 --> 00:47:21.752
No other ostriches have got dragons in their families.

00:47:21.812 --> 00:47:25.404
Chapter 13.

00:47:25.424 --> 00:47:33.172
Magic.

00:47:33.232 --> 00:47:39.000
We wake up and open our eyes.

00:47:39.060 --> 00:47:40.992
It is morning.

00:47:41.052 --> 00:47:44.464
It is sunny and warm again.

00:47:44.524 --> 00:47:48.786
Let's play tag, says Smiley.

00:47:48.846 --> 00:47:53.400
She likes playing tag because she runs very fast.

00:47:53.460 --> 00:47:58.102
She runs faster than dragon, dumpty and me.

00:47:58.162 --> 00:48:01.816
Okay, say dumpty and I.

00:48:01.876 --> 00:48:03.976
We look at dragon.

00:48:04.036 --> 00:48:07.071
She's shaking again.

00:48:07.131 --> 00:48:11.408
Why are you laughing at us again, we ask?

00:48:11.468 --> 00:48:15.982
I'm not laughing at you, says a strange voice.

00:48:16.042 --> 00:48:18.144
It isn't Dragon's voice.

00:48:18.204 --> 00:48:24.030
Her voice is high and loud, and this voice is low and quiet.

00:48:24.090 --> 00:48:25.851
We're afraid.

00:48:25.912 --> 00:48:28.694
Who's speaking, we ask?

00:48:28.754 --> 00:48:33.344
It's me, answers the strange voice.

00:48:33.404 --> 00:48:39.532
We look around, but we only can see mum, dad and dragon.

00:48:39.592 --> 00:48:43.002
Suddenly, smiley cries.

00:48:43.062 --> 00:48:45.324
It's dragon's voice.

00:48:45.384 --> 00:48:48.194
She's got a new voice.

00:48:48.254 --> 00:48:52.236
It's magic, says Dumpty.

00:48:52.296 --> 00:48:54.426
We look at dragon.

00:48:54.486 --> 00:48:56.187
She looks strange.

00:48:56.247 --> 00:49:00.695
She's shaking, and her eyes are very bright.

00:49:00.755 --> 00:49:03.824
Mum, cry smiley.

00:49:03.884 --> 00:49:06.536
What's the matter with dragon?

00:49:06.596 --> 00:49:09.448
Mum comes up to dragon.

00:49:09.508 --> 00:49:16.744
She looks at her, touches her head and says, dragon, you are ill.

00:49:16.804 --> 00:49:18.696
You have got a cold.

00:49:18.756 --> 00:49:21.228
You've got a high temperature.

00:49:21.288 --> 00:49:25.192
I have got a headache and a sore throat.

00:49:25.252 --> 00:49:29.646
So it's poor dragon and sneezes.

00:49:29.706 --> 00:49:34.288
And your nose is running, says Dad.

00:49:34.348 --> 00:49:36.978
It's the rain.

00:49:37.038 --> 00:49:41.049
Rain's are very cold in Africa.

00:49:41.109 --> 00:49:44.690
You must never dance in the rain again.

00:49:44.750 --> 00:49:47.170
It's dangerous.

00:49:47.230 --> 00:49:50.121
We are sorry for Dragon.

00:49:50.181 --> 00:49:56.402
She's sometimes very bad, but now she's so sad.

00:49:56.462 --> 00:50:00.579
Don't be sad, Dragon, says Dumpty.

00:50:00.639 --> 00:50:02.746
We like your new voice.

00:50:02.806 --> 00:50:05.448
It's so quiet.

00:50:05.508 --> 00:50:09.310
But Dragon isn't happy.

00:50:09.370 --> 00:50:12.162
She starts crying.

00:50:12.222 --> 00:50:17.696
We can bring you some sweet seeds, says Dumpty.

00:50:17.756 --> 00:50:27.837
I think it's very boring to be ill, so we can stay with you all day, smile smiley, and tell you funny stories.

00:50:27.897 --> 00:50:36.475
and bring you water from the river," I say, and brush your feathers for you, smile smiley.

00:50:36.535 --> 00:50:38.896
What's the matter?

00:50:38.956 --> 00:50:42.357
Dragon looks very strange again.

00:50:42.417 --> 00:50:44.988
I can't understand why.

00:50:45.048 --> 00:50:50.838
I look and look, and suddenly I understand.

00:50:50.899 --> 00:50:54.448
dragon is smiling.

00:50:54.508 --> 00:50:57.460
She's got a new face now.

00:50:57.520 --> 00:51:00.501
A kind, cute face.

00:51:00.561 --> 00:51:03.922
Oh, it's magic.

00:51:03.982 --> 00:51:16.292
Chapter 14 A new name.

00:51:16.352 --> 00:51:23.850
So we stay with dragon all day.

00:51:23.910 --> 00:51:33.138
Sometimes dumpty goes and brings sweet seeds, or I go to the river and bring some water in my beak for dragon.

00:51:33.198 --> 00:51:39.934
Smiley tells stories to her and brushes dragon's feathers.

00:51:39.994 --> 00:51:43.664
Mums stays with dragon too.

00:51:43.725 --> 00:51:51.484
She keeps her warm when dragon starts shaking and covers her from the sun.

00:51:51.544 --> 00:51:54.864
Dragon is better now.

00:51:54.924 --> 00:52:02.246
She listens to smiley, eats the seeds and drinks the water.

00:52:02.306 --> 00:52:05.956
She isn't shaking anymore.

00:52:06.016 --> 00:52:10.870
Suddenly, I can hear a voice.

00:52:10.930 --> 00:52:12.904
I know this voice.

00:52:12.964 --> 00:52:14.444
I like it.

00:52:14.504 --> 00:52:17.658
It is my favorite voice.

00:52:17.718 --> 00:52:20.060
Hello.

00:52:20.120 --> 00:52:23.332
Why are you not playing today?

00:52:23.393 --> 00:52:25.444
Asks the voice.

00:52:25.504 --> 00:52:29.618
I turn round and see softy.

00:52:29.678 --> 00:52:31.996
I am very happy.

00:52:32.056 --> 00:52:36.444
And I say, because dragon is ill.

00:52:36.504 --> 00:52:40.598
Suddenly, Softie is very sad.

00:52:40.658 --> 00:52:43.090
I know, she says.

00:52:43.150 --> 00:52:45.332
You don't want to play with me.

00:52:45.392 --> 00:52:47.313
You don't like me.

00:52:47.374 --> 00:52:49.595
I'm going away.

00:52:49.655 --> 00:52:52.988
She turns and starts walking away.

00:52:53.048 --> 00:52:55.330
Softie, please.

00:52:55.390 --> 00:52:57.641
Don't go away, I cry.

00:52:57.701 --> 00:52:58.842
I like you.

00:52:58.902 --> 00:53:00.590
You're so nice.

00:53:00.650 --> 00:53:03.968
Why do you always run away?

00:53:04.028 --> 00:53:09.880
But, say Softy, what about dragons?

00:53:09.940 --> 00:53:16.662
Why do you always talk about dragons when I want to play with you?

00:53:16.723 --> 00:53:22.715
Because dragon is our sister, I say.

00:53:22.775 --> 00:53:25.446
What?

00:53:25.506 --> 00:53:31.130
Softy's eyes become bigger than her head.

00:53:31.190 --> 00:53:35.173
Look, here she is, I say.

00:53:35.233 --> 00:53:37.354
She's ill today.

00:53:37.414 --> 00:53:42.906
We're staying with her, because it's very boring to be ill.

00:53:42.966 --> 00:53:46.467
Softy looks at dragon.

00:53:46.527 --> 00:53:51.078
Dragon isn't that old dragon anymore.

00:53:51.138 --> 00:53:53.630
She's new dragon now.

00:53:53.690 --> 00:53:56.940
She's got a kind smile.

00:53:57.000 --> 00:53:59.452
Are you dragon?

00:53:59.512 --> 00:54:01.922
Ask Softy.

00:54:01.982 --> 00:54:06.284
Yes, I am, answers dragon.

00:54:06.344 --> 00:54:12.048
But dragons are ugly, angry monsters, say softy.

00:54:12.108 --> 00:54:13.218
What?

00:54:13.278 --> 00:54:15.970
cries dragon.

00:54:16.030 --> 00:54:19.982
We can't see her smile anymore.

00:54:20.042 --> 00:54:23.444
She's our old dragon now.

00:54:23.504 --> 00:54:27.688
I'm not an ugly, angry monster.

00:54:27.748 --> 00:54:32.412
And you are, dragon, says Meng.

00:54:32.472 --> 00:54:35.544
That ostrich girl is right.

00:54:35.604 --> 00:54:40.315
Dragon means a terrible ugly monster.

00:54:40.375 --> 00:54:43.545
It likes eating other animals.

00:54:43.606 --> 00:54:46.686
It can even eat an ostrich.

00:54:46.746 --> 00:54:50.888
I think you should change your name.

00:54:50.948 --> 00:54:59.310
Oh, now I understand why you always run away, I say, to softy.

00:54:59.370 --> 00:55:01.927
Then it's true.

00:55:01.987 --> 00:55:07.527
You like me and want to play with me, smile softy.

00:55:07.588 --> 00:55:11.300
Of course, I smile at her.

00:55:11.360 --> 00:55:14.793
Dragon is very quiet now.

00:55:14.853 --> 00:55:16.554
She looks at us.

00:55:16.614 --> 00:55:18.656
She looks at mum.

00:55:18.716 --> 00:55:25.020
And then she says, I don't want to be dragon anymore.

00:55:25.080 --> 00:55:28.332
Help me to find a nice name.

00:55:28.392 --> 00:55:31.904
We can't believe our ears.

00:55:31.964 --> 00:55:37.665
Dragon is really asking us to help her.

00:55:37.725 --> 00:55:40.766
Do you like the sun?

00:55:40.826 --> 00:55:42.538
Asks mum.

00:55:42.598 --> 00:55:44.999
Yes, I like it.

00:55:45.059 --> 00:55:51.502
It is very hot and dries us when we are wet, says Dragon and coughs.

00:55:51.562 --> 00:55:54.534
Do you want to be sunny?

00:55:54.594 --> 00:55:56.586
Asks mum.

00:55:56.646 --> 00:55:59.437
Oh, that's great, cries dragon.

00:55:59.497 --> 00:56:01.688
I like this name.

00:56:01.748 --> 00:56:05.290
Our dragon likes something.

00:56:05.350 --> 00:56:07.190
It is magic.

00:56:07.250 --> 00:56:08.952
Oh, I'm wrong.

00:56:09.012 --> 00:56:11.893
Our sister isn't dragon anymore.

00:56:11.954 --> 00:56:15.356
Now she is sunny.

00:56:15.416 --> 00:56:18.217
Chapter 15.

00:56:18.278 --> 00:56:20.879
A big day.

00:56:20.919 --> 00:56:28.522
Look at us.

00:56:28.582 --> 00:56:34.364
We're bigger now.

00:56:34.424 --> 00:56:36.914
Our legs are stronger.

00:56:36.974 --> 00:56:44.398
Dumpty is taller than Dad, and smiley is fatter than Mum.

00:56:44.458 --> 00:56:47.970
We are almost grown-ups.

00:56:48.030 --> 00:56:51.701
We don't walk with Mum and Dad anymore.

00:56:51.761 --> 00:56:55.872
We walk with other young ostriches.

00:56:55.932 --> 00:57:00.278
There are a lot of them in our group.

00:57:00.338 --> 00:57:03.724
Softy is with us too.

00:57:03.784 --> 00:57:05.174
No.

00:57:05.234 --> 00:57:07.966
She is with me.

00:57:08.026 --> 00:57:11.958
We want to be together all our life.

00:57:12.018 --> 00:57:14.450
We want to have a family.

00:57:14.510 --> 00:57:18.302
We want to have sons and daughters.

00:57:18.362 --> 00:57:27.048
I want to call my son and daughter, dumpedy and smiley, because I love my brother and sister.

00:57:27.108 --> 00:57:31.116
Softy has got a brother and sister too.

00:57:31.176 --> 00:57:35.292
Their names are foodie and tallie.

00:57:35.352 --> 00:57:42.696
It is because her brother likes eating and her sister is the tallest in the family.

00:57:42.756 --> 00:57:49.068
She is even taller than her father.

00:57:49.128 --> 00:57:54.251
Two months pass.

00:57:54.311 --> 00:57:59.014
Softie and I have got a nest now.

00:57:59.074 --> 00:58:01.770
It is on the ground.

00:58:01.830 --> 00:58:05.166
There are three eggs in the nest.

00:58:05.226 --> 00:58:11.550
I guard our chicks at night, and softy does it by day.

00:58:11.610 --> 00:58:14.472
The great day comes.

00:58:14.533 --> 00:58:21.727
The first egg breaks into small pieces, and we can see our sun.

00:58:21.787 --> 00:58:26.320
He has got very big feet.

00:58:26.380 --> 00:58:32.502
Our sun is very clever, left softy.

00:58:32.562 --> 00:58:35.762
Why, I ask?

00:58:35.822 --> 00:58:38.083
He knows our problem.

00:58:38.143 --> 00:58:45.988
Look, he's got very big feet, so his name must be footy.

00:58:46.049 --> 00:58:49.982
It's half foodie and half dumpty.

00:58:50.042 --> 00:58:53.663
Our good boy, I smile.

00:58:53.724 --> 00:59:00.383
Here comes our daughter, say softy, when the second egg breaks.

00:59:00.443 --> 00:59:03.620
Why is she so small?

00:59:03.680 --> 00:59:04.600
I ask.

00:59:04.660 --> 00:59:06.851
I'm worried.

00:59:06.912 --> 00:59:09.973
Don't worry, say softy.

00:59:10.033 --> 00:59:12.004
She must be small.

00:59:12.064 --> 00:59:13.005
Why?

00:59:13.025 --> 00:59:14.996
I ask again.

00:59:15.056 --> 00:59:18.007
Think dear, say softy.

00:59:18.068 --> 00:59:20.458
I think and think.

00:59:20.518 --> 00:59:23.544
And then I understand.

00:59:23.604 --> 00:59:28.030
It's because her name must be smally.

00:59:28.090 --> 00:59:31.962
It's half smiley and half tally.

00:59:32.022 --> 00:59:34.986
Yes, say softy.

00:59:35.046 --> 00:59:39.999
Our children are very young but very clever.

00:59:40.059 --> 00:59:42.430
We look at the third egg.

00:59:42.490 --> 00:59:45.143
It is breaking now too.

00:59:45.203 --> 00:59:49.256
Our second daughter is coming out.

00:59:49.316 --> 00:59:52.500
She is cute.

00:59:52.560 --> 00:59:58.474
She has got yellow feathers and a long slim neck.

00:59:58.534 --> 01:00:03.456
Let's call her slimmy, say softy.

01:00:03.516 --> 01:00:06.777
No, says our daughter.

01:00:06.837 --> 01:00:09.208
I don't like this name.

01:00:09.268 --> 01:00:12.720
What about yellow?

01:00:12.780 --> 01:00:13.960
I ask.

01:00:14.020 --> 01:00:17.562
No, she says again.

01:00:17.622 --> 01:00:21.124
Oh, no, I cry.

01:00:21.184 --> 01:00:23.184
It's dragon.

01:00:23.245 --> 01:00:28.388
Our daughter looks at the sky and sees the sun.

01:00:28.448 --> 01:00:29.750
What is this?

01:00:29.810 --> 01:00:31.140
She asks.

01:00:31.200 --> 01:00:34.844
It's the sun answers softly.

01:00:34.904 --> 01:00:38.076
I am very quiet now.

01:00:38.136 --> 01:00:41.350
I am looking at my daughter.

01:00:41.410 --> 01:00:44.902
I can see her nice face.

01:00:44.962 --> 01:00:48.235
Of course she isn't dragon.

01:00:48.295 --> 01:00:53.712
My name is Sunny, she says.

01:00:53.772 --> 01:00:55.419
and smiles.

